   The lock moves matplotlib, tensorboard to an older version to fit the fixes together: check that before merging. In a lock forked by Python version this is usually the copy for the oldest Python you support; raising requires-python (see Python floor) may avoid it.

   Python floor:
     Raising requires-python to >=3.11 would let 1 fix install (filelock; 4 alerts), verified with uv's resolver.
     It drops Python 3.10: fine for an application, a breaking change for users of a published library.
     Add --raise-python-floor to put that change in the plan.

   Dependabot resolves for the oldest Python requires-python allows (3.10) and filters out releases that need a newer one: pillow 13.0.0 needs Python >=3.11. uv locks them only for the Pythons they support.

   Verified with uv's resolver: 15 of 17 fixes resolve together, plus 1 partial fix on your current Python range.
